# Build context for infra/docker/python.Dockerfile (context = repository root).
#
# Allowlist: everything is excluded except what the Python image needs. This keeps the context
# small and guarantees that .env files, local-sources/ (model weights, datasets), runtime data,
# node_modules and the git history never reach the build context or an image layer.
# The web image builds from apps/web with infra/docker/web.Dockerfile.dockerignore instead.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!packages/
!services/
!profiles/

# Never include caches, virtualenvs, local secrets or editor state from the allowed trees.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.venv
**/.venv*
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
